<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 74.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Nominal Holocene point (a=0.073, b=1.186, Du=0.031, Dv=1.742, gamma=6) selects k*=6.135 with simulated dominant wavelength 431.3 µm against the 436 µm slot scale (about 1.1 percent). Equal diffusion is linearly stable. An 80 µm cellular predecessor cannot fit one wave (fundamental growth rate about -29). A 4360 µm successor flank holds ten wavelengths of the same k*; there is no second Felis chronospecies (series 1/1, age 0 Ma). The rendered patch is an isotropic spot lattice, not the mackerel stripes of the photographed tabby. Pass 1 does not yet sweep Dv, simulate an ablation, report specimen-segmentation statistics, or give Pearson/RMSE/KS for the dispersion relation. Overall 74.6/100 (faithfulness 70.1, reproducibility 84.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 64, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: docs/media/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 715098 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 128af19622dfeb40bb71adf27ba03329ac40dcec545c031314a81f264362e19c (sha256 128af19622dfeb40bb71adf27ba03329ac40dcec545c031314a81f264362e19c), spec_fingerprint dc73277e26df9e4f2f17850cccebf7acc56dadcc0fc11952482db451621788f3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dc73277e26df9e4f2f17850cccebf7acc56dadcc0fc11952482db451621788f3; artifact_sha256: 128af19622dfeb40bb71adf27ba03329ac40dcec545c031314a81f264362e19c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0/felis_catus_specimen.jpg=9360be6f1689a1df..., datasets/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a7694c1c70d27f08...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous RD system can be unstable at a finite wavenumber. | Murray 1981: coat markings can be a chemical pre-pattern whose repeat count tracks domain size over wavelength. | Kaelin 2012: Taqpep sets a periodic pre-pattern in fetal cat skin; Edn3 implements pigment. | Kaelin 2021: a Dkk4 pre-pattern precedes visible stripes in fetal domestic-cat epidermis.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics as a minimal two-species realisation of k* selection, calibrated so lambda(k*) = 436 µm. | Spectral operator-split integration on a periodic 5-wave patch. | Registration of that patch onto a CC BY-SA photograph of an adult tabby.; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma) are not measured Dkk4 or Wnt rate constants. | The photograph is the expanded Holocene phenotype, not a 436 µm micrograph.; does_not_claim: That 436 µm was measured by Kaelin, Murray, or Turing. | That this isotropic spot lattice is the mackerel-tabby pattern of the photographed cat. | A predecessor Felis chronospecies. The series is 1/1 at 0 Ma.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-ablation', 'item': 'Simulate the equal-diffusion negative control and an ablation that removes the u^2 v term. Pass 1 only checks the analytic sign of sigma.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-assessor', 'item': 'Single builder-assessor. No independent second assessor.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-gof', 'item': 'Goodness of fit of the dispersion relation: Pearson r, RMSE, and a KS statistic between analytic sigma(k) and a numerical linear integration. Require Pearson r > 0.98.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-segment', 'item': 'Report specimen CV segmentation metrics (foreground fraction, circularity, structure-tensor coherency, aspect) measured on the real photograph, with references that are not copies of the values.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-stripes', 'item': 'The isotropic patch is a spot lattice. The photographed cat is a broken mackerel tabby. Either bias the pattern toward stripes or keep the spot reading explicit.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-sweep', 'item': 'Sweep inhibitor diffusion Dv and report k* and lambda at each value. Pass 1 only evaluates the nominal point.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 7.46e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

