<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 1) (Felis catus (domestic cat))",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 1) faithfully reproduces Felis catus (domestic cat) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Felis catus (domestic cat) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Felis catus (domestic cat)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A predecessor Felis chronospecies. The series is 1/1 at 0 Ma.",
        "does_not_claim: That 436 µm was measured by Kaelin, Murray, or Turing.",
        "does_not_claim: That this isotropic spot lattice is the mackerel-tabby pattern of the photographed cat.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Registration of that patch onto a CC BY-SA photograph of an adult tabby.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics as a minimal two-species realisation of k* selection, calibrated so lambda(k*) = 436 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral operator-split integration on a periodic 5-wave patch.",
        "reported_in_source: Kaelin 2012: Taqpep sets a periodic pre-pattern in fetal cat skin; Edn3 implements pigment.",
        "reported_in_source: Kaelin 2021: a Dkk4 pre-pattern precedes visible stripes in fetal domestic-cat epidermis.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: coat markings can be a chemical pre-pattern whose repeat count tracks domain size over wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous RD system can be unstable at a finite wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma) are not measured Dkk4 or Wnt rate constants.",
        "transfer_boundary: The photograph is the expanded Holocene phenotype, not a 436 µm micrograph." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Felis catus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Felis" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Felis catus (domestic cat); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a homogeneous RD system can be unstable at a finite wavenumber. | Murray 1981: coat markings can be a chemical pre-pattern whose repeat count tracks domain size over wavelength. | Kaelin 2012: Taqpep sets a periodic pre-pattern in fetal cat skin; Edn3 implements pigment. | Kaelin 2021: a Dkk4 pre-pattern precedes visible stripes in fetal domestic-cat epidermis.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics as a minimal two-species realisation of k* selection, calibrated so lambda(k*) = 436 µm. | Spectral operator-split integration on a periodic 5-wave patch. | Registration of that patch onto a CC BY-SA photograph of an adult tabby.; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg (a, b, Du, Dv, gamma) are not measured Dkk4 or Wnt rate constants. | The photograph is the expanded Holocene phenotype, not a 436 µm micrograph.; does_not_claim: That 436 µm was measured by Kaelin, Murray, or Turing. | That this isotropic spot lattice is the mackerel-tabby pattern of the photographed cat. | A predecessor Felis chronospecies. The series is 1/1 at 0 Ma.]; phenomenon_size: 335 µm (0.0003348 m, log10=-3.475 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 335 µm to 98.0 cm): 335 µm:felis-catus-bioelectric-polarity, 1.2 mm:felis-catus-vertex-packing, 2.2 cm:felis-catus-turing-wavelength, 4.1 cm:felis-catus-clock-wavefront, 7.0 cm:felis-catus-morphogen-condensation, 8.9 cm:felis-catus-flux-canalization, 9.9 cm:felis-catus-elastic-buckling, 11.3 cm:felis-catus-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-021-25348-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1220893> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
    pk:geologicalPeriod "Holocene (Extant)" ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
